  "witnessed_boundary": {
    "wsl_driver_bridge_boundary": {
      "summary": "WSL2 exposes /dev/dxg and /usr/lib/wsl/lib/libd3d12core.so, but lacks /dev/kfd and /dev/dri.",
      "detail": "AMD ROCm Linux userspace driver requires /dev/kfd (Kernel Fusion Driver) and DRM render nodes (/dev/dri/renderD*), which are not bridged through standard WSL2 WDDM for AMD consumer RDNA3 gfx1102. Unlike NVIDIA NVML/CUDA which has a /dev/dxg CUDA driver translation layer (libcuda.so), AMD's experimental WSL2 bridge (librocdxg) fails adapter query IOCTLs (-22, -2) against consumer Windows driver 32.0.31041.1004, causing HSA initialization to fail with 'No WDDM adapters found'."
    },
